IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore): s 4 outside its list of defined terms -- the opening words of s 4(1), and s 4(3) to (13), the rules
-- of reading and the deeming provisions. (s 4(2) sits beside "director" in sg-definitions.)
--
-- Every function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN. Where a subsection says "unless the contrary intention appears" the contrary intention is a
-- plain input (a reader of the provision where the word is used can say whether one appears); a contrary intention is the text's
-- own "no" (it says "unless"). Where a subsection deems or includes and the case is outside what it names, the answer is NOTHING:
-- the subsection adds to the ordinary meaning; it does not take away.

§ `Section 4(1): the opening words`

-- src:1139 | 4.—(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears —
@ref s 4(1) (src:1139-1139)
GIVEN `the word is one that subsection (1) defines` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the word is used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) the definition in subsection (1) governs the word where it is used` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the word is one that subsection (1) defines`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the opening words speak of the defined terms only
    ELSE (IF `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the word is used`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

§ `Section 4(3) and (4): the statement in lieu of prospectus`

-- (3): a statement in a statement in lieu of prospectus is deemed untrue if it is misleading in the form and context in which it is included.
-- src:1811 | (3) For the purposes of this Act, a statement included in a statement
-- src:1812 | in lieu of prospectus is deemed to be untrue if it is misleading in the
-- src:1813 | form and context in which it is included.
@ref s 4(3) (src:1811-1813)
GIVEN `the statement is included in a statement in lieu of prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is misleading in the form and context in which it is included` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(3) the statement is deemed to be untrue` MEANS
    IF `the statement is included in a statement in lieu of prospectus` AND `the statement is misleading in the form and context in which it is included`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to be untrue if it is misleading in the form and context in which it is included" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a); a statement may still be untrue in fact: NOTES.md)

-- (4): a statement is deemed included in a statement in lieu of prospectus if it is contained in a report or memorandum appearing on the face of it,
-- incorporated in it by reference, or issued with it.
-- src:1817 | (4) For the purposes of this Act, a statement is deemed to be
-- src:1818 | included in a statement in lieu of prospectus if it is contained in any
-- src:1819 | report or memorandum appearing on the face thereof or by reference
-- src:1820 | incorporated therein or issued therewith.
@ref s 4(4) (src:1817-1820)
GIVEN `the statement is contained in a report or memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report or memorandum appears on the face of the statement in lieu of prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report or memorandum is incorporated in the statement in lieu of prospectus by reference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report or memorandum is issued with the statement in lieu of prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(4) the statement is deemed to be included in a statement in lieu of prospectus` MEANS
    IF    `the statement is contained in a report or memorandum`
      AND (    `the report or memorandum appears on the face of the statement in lieu of prospectus`
            OR `the report or memorandum is incorporated in the statement in lieu of prospectus by reference`
            OR `the report or memorandum is issued with the statement in lieu of prospectus`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to be included in a statement in lieu of prospectus if it is contained in any report or memorandum appearing on the face thereof or by reference incorporated therein or issued therewith" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

§ `Section 4(5) and (5A): invitations to deposit or lend, and the debenture`

-- (5): an invitation to the public to deposit money with, or lend money to, a corporation is deemed an invitation to subscribe for or purchase
-- debentures, other than where the corporation is a prescribed entity mentioned in s 239(4) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001.
-- (The parenthesis around the exclusion is not closed in the text as rendered: NOTES.md, finding.)
-- src:1825 | (5) For the purposes of this Act, any invitation to the public to
-- src:1826 | deposit money with or lend money to a corporation (other than a
-- src:1827 | corporation that is a prescribed entity mentioned in section 239(4) of
-- src:1828 | the Securities and Futures Act 2001 is deemed to be an invitation to
-- src:1829 | subscribe for or purchase debentures of the corporation.
@ref s 4(5) (src:1825-1829)
GIVEN `the invitation is an invitation to the public to deposit money with or lend money to a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is a prescribed entity mentioned in section 239(4) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(5) the invitation is deemed to be an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures of the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the invitation is an invitation to the public to deposit money with or lend money to a corporation`
    THEN (IF `the corporation is a prescribed entity mentioned in section 239(4) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(other than a corporation that is a prescribed entity mentioned in section 239(4) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection deems only an invitation to the public to deposit money with or lend money to a corporation

-- (5A): a document acknowledging the indebtedness for money deposited or lent in response to such an invitation is deemed a debenture.
-- src:1831 | (5A) For the purposes of this Act, any document that is issued or
-- src:1832 | intended or required to be issued by a corporation acknowledging or
-- src:1833 | evidencing or constituting an acknowledgment of the indebtedness of
-- src:1834 | the corporation in respect of any money that is or may be deposited
-- src:1835 | with or lent to the corporation in response to such an invitation is
-- src:1836 | deemed to be a debenture.
@ref s 4(5A) (src:1831-1836)
GIVEN `the document is issued, or is intended or required to be issued, by a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document acknowledges or evidences or constitutes an acknowledgment of the indebtedness of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indebtedness is in respect of money that is or may be deposited with or lent to the corporation in response to an invitation that subsection (5) treats as an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(5A) the document is deemed to be a debenture` MEANS
    IF    `the document is issued, or is intended or required to be issued, by a corporation`
      AND `the document acknowledges or evidences or constitutes an acknowledgment of the indebtedness of the corporation`
      AND `the indebtedness is in respect of money that is or may be deposited with or lent to the corporation in response to an invitation that subsection (5) treats as an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any document that is issued or intended or required to be issued by a corporation acknowledging ... in response to such an invitation is deemed to be a debenture" says nothing of another document

§ `Section 4(6) and (7): bankruptcy references`

-- (6) reads "[Deleted by Act 42 of 2001]": nothing to encode (NOTES.md coverage row: repealed).

-- (7): a reference to bankruptcy is read as including the corresponding insolvency under any written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency.
-- One function per kind of reference the subsection names; the facts are the person's, stated as a witness would.
-- src:1840 | (7) Unless the contrary intention appears, any reference in this Act
-- src:1841 | to a person being or becoming bankrupt or to a person assigning the
-- src:1842 | person’s estate for the benefit of the person’s creditors or making an
-- src:1843 | arrangement with the person’s creditors under any written law
-- src:1844 | relating to bankruptcy or to a person being an undischarged bankrupt
-- src:1845 | or to any status, condition, act, matter or thing under or in relation to
-- src:1846 | the law of bankruptcy is to be construed as including a reference to a
-- src:1847 | person being or becoming bankrupt or insolvent or to a person
-- src:1852 | making any such assignment or arrangement or to a person being an
-- src:1853 | undischarged bankrupt or insolvent or to the corresponding status,
-- src:1854 | condition, act, matter or thing (as the case requires) under any written
-- src:1855 | law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency.
@ref s 4(7) (src:1840-1855)
GIVEN `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the reference is used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is, or is becoming, bankrupt or insolvent under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(7) a reference to a person being or becoming bankrupt covers the person being or becoming insolvent` MEANS
    IF `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the reference is used`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the contrary intention appears, any reference in this Act to a person being or becoming bankrupt ... is to be construed as including"
    ELSE (IF `the person is, or is becoming, bankrupt or insolvent under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "is to be construed as including a reference to a person being or becoming bankrupt or insolvent" adds to the ordinary meaning

@ref s 4(7) (src:1840-1855)
GIVEN `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the reference is used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has made an assignment of the person's estate for the benefit of the person's creditors, or an arrangement with the person's creditors, under any written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(7) a reference to a person assigning the person's estate for the benefit of creditors or making an arrangement with them covers the same under any written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` MEANS
    IF `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the reference is used`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the contrary intention appears"
    ELSE (IF `the person has made an assignment of the person's estate for the benefit of the person's creditors, or an arrangement with the person's creditors, under any written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "to a person making any such assignment or arrangement" under any such law adds to the ordinary meaning

@ref s 4(7) (src:1840-1855)
GIVEN `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the reference is used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(7) a reference to a person being an undischarged bankrupt covers the person being an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent` MEANS
    IF `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the reference is used`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the contrary intention appears"
    ELSE (IF `the person is an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "or to a person being an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent" adds to the ordinary meaning

@ref s 4(7) (src:1840-1855)
GIVEN `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the reference is used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the status, condition, act, matter or thing corresponds to one under or in relation to the law of bankruptcy, and arises under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(7) a reference to a status, condition, act, matter or thing under the law of bankruptcy covers the corresponding one under any written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` MEANS
    IF `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the reference is used`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the contrary intention appears"
    ELSE (IF `the status, condition, act, matter or thing corresponds to one under or in relation to the law of bankruptcy, and arises under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "or to the corresponding status, condition, act, matter or thing (as the case requires) under any written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency" adds to the ordinary meaning

§ `Section 4(8) and (9): the affairs of a corporation`

-- The list of (8), paragraph by paragraph. Some paragraphs carry a condition of their own; the three conditions are inputs to the function below.
DECLARE `s 4(8) matter`
    IS ONE OF
        `s 4(8)(a) the promotion, formation, membership, control, business, trading, transactions, dealings, property, liabilities, profits, income, receipts, losses, outgoings or expenditure of the corporation`
        `s 4(8)(b) the identity of the beneficiaries under a trust of which the corporation is trustee, their rights and the payments they have received or are entitled to receive`
        `s 4(8)(c) the internal management and proceeding of the corporation`
        `s 4(8)(d) an act or thing done by or on behalf of the corporation, or to or in relation to it or its business or property, at a time when it was in receivership, under judicial management, administering a compromise or arrangement, or being wound up`
        `s 4(8)(d) the conduct of a receiver, a receiver and manager, a judicial manager, a person administering a compromise or arrangement, a liquidator or a provisional liquidator of the corporation`
        `s 4(8)(e) the ownership of shares in, debentures of, and interests issued by, the corporation`
        `s 4(8)(f) the power of persons to exercise, or to control the exercise of, voting rights attached to shares in the corporation or to dispose of, or to control the disposal of, such shares`
        `s 4(8)(g) the ascertainment of the persons who are or have been financially interested in the success or failure of the corporation or able to control or materially influence its policy`
        `s 4(8)(h) the circumstances under which a person acquired or disposed of, or became entitled to acquire or dispose of, shares in, debentures of, or interests issued by, the corporation`
        `s 4(8)(i) the financial or business undertaking, scheme, common enterprise or investment contract to which interests issued by the corporation relate`
        `s 4(8)(j) the audit of, or working papers or reports of an auditor concerning, a matter referred to in paragraphs (a) to (i)`
        `s 4(8) some other matter`

-- The paragraphs themselves. A paragraph that carries a condition of its own (b, d, i) answers NOTHING where the condition fails: it
-- names its own case, and says nothing outside it.
-- src:1863 | (a) the promotion, formation, membership, control, business,
-- src:1864 | trading, transactions and dealings (whether alone or jointly
-- src:1865 | with another person or other persons and including
-- src:1866 | transactions and dealings as agent, bailee or trustee),
-- src:1867 | property (whether held alone or jointly with another person
-- src:1868 | or other persons and including property held as agent,
-- src:1869 | bailee or trustee), liabilities (including liabilities owed
-- src:1870 | jointly with another person or other persons and liabilities
-- src:1871 | as trustee), profits and other income, receipts, losses,
-- src:1872 | outgoings and expenditure of the corporation;
-- src:1874 | (b) in the case of a corporation (not being a trustee
-- src:1875 | corporation) that is a trustee (but without limiting
-- src:1876 | paragraph (a)), matters concerned with the ascertainment
-- src:1877 | of the identity of the persons who are beneficiaries under
-- src:1878 | the trust, their rights under the trust and any payments that
-- src:1879 | they have received, or are entitled to receive, under the
-- src:1880 | terms of the trust;
-- src:1882 | (c) the internal management and proceeding of the
-- src:1883 | corporation;
-- src:1885 | (d) any act or thing done (including any contract made and any
-- src:1886 | transaction entered into) by or on behalf of the corporation,
-- src:1887 | or to or in relation to the corporation or its business or
-- src:1888 | property, at a time when —
-- src:1890 | (i) a receiver, or a receiver and manager, is in possession
-- src:1891 | of, or has control over, property of the corporation;
-- src:1893 | (ii) the corporation is under judicial management;
-- src:1898 | (iii) a compromise or an arrangement made between the
-- src:1899 | corporation and another person or other persons is
-- src:1900 | being administered; or
-- src:1902 | (iv) the corporation is being wound up,
-- src:1904 | (d) and, without limiting the foregoing, any conduct of such a
-- src:1905 | receiver or such a receiver and manager, or such a judicial
-- src:1906 | manager, of any person administering such a compromise
-- src:1907 | or arrangement or of any liquidator or provisional
-- src:1908 | liquidator of the corporation;
-- src:1910 | (e) the ownership of shares in, debentures of, and interests
-- src:1911 | issued by, the corporation;
-- src:1913 | (f) the power of persons to exercise, or to control the exercise
-- src:1914 | of, the rights to vote attached to shares in the corporation or
-- src:1915 | to dispose of, or to exercise control over the disposal of,
-- src:1916 | such shares;
-- src:1918 | (g) matters concerned with the ascertainment of the persons
-- src:1919 | who are or have been financially interested in the success
-- src:1920 | or failure, or apparent success or failure, of the corporation
-- src:1921 | or are or have been able to control or materially to
-- src:1922 | influence the policy of the corporation;
-- src:1924 | (h) the circumstances under which a person acquired or
-- src:1925 | disposed of, or became entitled to acquire or dispose of,
-- src:1926 | shares in, debentures of, or interests issued by, the
-- src:1927 | corporation;
-- src:1929 | (i) where the corporation has issued interests, any matters
-- src:1930 | concerning the financial or business undertaking, scheme,
-- src:1931 | common enterprise or investment contract to which the
-- src:1932 | interests relate; and
-- src:1934 | (j) matters relating to or arising out of the audit of, or working
-- src:1935 | papers or reports of an auditor concerning, any matters
-- src:1936 | referred to in any of the preceding paragraphs.
@ref s 4(8)(a) to (j) (src:1863-1936)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 4(8) matter`
      `the corporation is a trustee and is not a trustee corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or thing was done at a time when a receiver, or a receiver and manager, was in possession of or had control over property of the corporation, the corporation was under judicial management, a compromise or an arrangement between the corporation and another person was being administered, or the corporation was being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has issued interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 4(8)(a) the promotion, formation, membership, control, business, trading, transactions, dealings, property, liabilities, profits, income, receipts, losses, outgoings or expenditure of the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4(8)(b) the identity of the beneficiaries under a trust of which the corporation is trustee, their rights and the payments they have received or are entitled to receive` THEN
        (IF `the corporation is a trustee and is not a trustee corporation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a corporation (not being a trustee corporation) that is a trustee"
    WHEN `s 4(8)(c) the internal management and proceeding of the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4(8)(d) an act or thing done by or on behalf of the corporation, or to or in relation to it or its business or property, at a time when it was in receivership, under judicial management, administering a compromise or arrangement, or being wound up` THEN
        (IF `the act or thing was done at a time when a receiver, or a receiver and manager, was in possession of or had control over property of the corporation, the corporation was under judicial management, a compromise or an arrangement between the corporation and another person was being administered, or the corporation was being wound up`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at a time when (i) a receiver ... (iv) the corporation is being wound up"
    WHEN `s 4(8)(d) the conduct of a receiver, a receiver and manager, a judicial manager, a person administering a compromise or arrangement, a liquidator or a provisional liquidator of the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4(8)(e) the ownership of shares in, debentures of, and interests issued by, the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4(8)(f) the power of persons to exercise, or to control the exercise of, voting rights attached to shares in the corporation or to dispose of, or to control the disposal of, such shares` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4(8)(g) the ascertainment of the persons who are or have been financially interested in the success or failure of the corporation or able to control or materially influence its policy` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4(8)(h) the circumstances under which a person acquired or disposed of, or became entitled to acquire or dispose of, shares in, debentures of, or interests issued by, the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4(8)(i) the financial or business undertaking, scheme, common enterprise or investment contract to which interests issued by the corporation relate` THEN
        (IF `the corporation has issued interests`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the corporation has issued interests"
    WHEN `s 4(8)(j) the audit of, or working papers or reports of an auditor concerning, a matter referred to in paragraphs (a) to (i)` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "is ... to be construed as including a reference to" the paragraphs leaves the list open

-- (8): the list applies to a reference in the sections it names, unless a contrary intention appears.
-- src:1859 | (8) A reference in section 8A, 8C, 8D, 216, Part 9 or section 402 to
-- src:1860 | the affairs of a corporation is, unless the contrary intention appears, to
-- src:1861 | be construed as including a reference to —
@ref s 4(8) (src:1859-1861)
GIVEN `the reference is in section 8A, 8C, 8D, 216, Part 9 or section 402` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the reference is used` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 4(8) matter`
      `the corporation is a trustee and is not a trustee corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or thing was done at a time when a receiver, or a receiver and manager, was in possession of or had control over property of the corporation, the corporation was under judicial management, a compromise or an arrangement between the corporation and another person was being administered, or the corporation was being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has issued interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(8) a reference to the affairs of a corporation covers the matter` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the reference is in section 8A, 8C, 8D, 216, Part 9 or section 402`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A reference in section 8A, 8C, 8D, 216, Part 9 or section 402 to the affairs of a corporation"; for a reference elsewhere subsection (9) may apply
    ELSE (IF `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the reference is used`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, unless the contrary intention appears, to be construed as including" (marginal reading (a): a contrary intention displaces the construction, not necessarily the ordinary meaning)
          ELSE `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` matter `the corporation is a trustee and is not a trustee corporation` `the act or thing was done at a time when a receiver, or a receiver and manager, was in possession of or had control over property of the corporation, the corporation was under judicial management, a compromise or an arrangement between the corporation and another person was being administered, or the corporation was being wound up` `the corporation has issued interests`)

-- (9): wherever the Act speaks of the affairs of a company or a foreign company, the (8) list applies, with no contrary-intention proviso.
-- src:1940 | (9) For the purposes of this Act, wherever a reference to the affairs
-- src:1941 | of a company or a foreign company appears it is to be construed as
-- src:1946 | including a reference to the affairs of a corporation as defined in
-- src:1947 | subsection (8).
@ref s 4(9) (src:1940-1947)
GIVEN `the reference is to the affairs of a company or a foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 4(8) matter`
      `the corporation is a trustee and is not a trustee corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or thing was done at a time when a receiver, or a receiver and manager, was in possession of or had control over property of the corporation, the corporation was under judicial management, a compromise or an arrangement between the corporation and another person was being administered, or the corporation was being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has issued interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(9) a reference to the affairs of a company or a foreign company covers the matter` MEANS
    IF `the reference is to the affairs of a company or a foreign company`
    THEN `s 4(8) the matter is one that the subsection says the affairs of a corporation include` matter `the corporation is a trustee and is not a trustee corporation` `the act or thing was done at a time when a receiver, or a receiver and manager, was in possession of or had control over property of the corporation, the corporation was under judicial management, a compromise or an arrangement between the corporation and another person was being administered, or the corporation was being wound up` `the corporation has issued interests`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "wherever a reference to the affairs of a company or a foreign company appears"

§ `Section 4(10) and (11): a company with one director`

-- src:1949 | (10) A reference in this Act to the directors of a company is, in the
-- src:1950 | case of a company which has only one director, to be construed as a
-- src:1951 | reference to that director.
@ref s 4(10) (src:1949-1951)
GIVEN `the number of directors of the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(10) a reference to the directors of the company is a reference to its only director` MEANS
    IF `the number of directors of the company` EQUALS 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, in the case of a company which has only one director, to be construed as a reference to that director" (a condition of the "where" kind: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-D6 in NOTES.md)

-- src:1953 | (11) A reference in this Act to the doing of any act by 2 or more
-- src:1954 | directors of a company is, in the case of a company which has only
-- src:1955 | one director, to be construed as the doing of that act by that director.
@ref s 4(11) (src:1953-1955)
GIVEN `the number of directors of the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the act has been done by the only director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(11) the act of the only director counts as the doing of the act by 2 or more directors` MEANS
    IF `the number of directors of the company` EQUALS 1
    THEN (IF `the act has been done by the only director of the company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says how an act of the only director is construed; it says nothing of a company with one director who has not done the act
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, in the case of a company which has only one director, to be construed as the doing of that act by that director" (a condition of the "where" kind: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-D6 in NOTES.md)

§ `Section 4(12): the Minister of State`

-- The sections the subsection lists, one string each, in the Act's own form (section number, then the subsection or paragraph in brackets).
-- src:1957 | (12) For the purposes of section 20(3), 27(2), (5), (5AA), (5A) or
-- src:1958 | (12C), 28(3), (3D), (3DA) or (3E), 29(8A), 155B(8), 359(9), 360(3),
-- src:1959 | 369(2), 377(13) or 378(5), (9) or (16), any reference to the Minister
-- src:1960 | includes a reference to a Minister of State for his or her Ministry who
-- src:1961 | is authorised by the Minister for the purposes of hearing an appeal
-- src:1962 | under that section.
@ref s 4(12) (src:1957-1962)
`s 4(12) the provisions in which a Minister of State may stand for the Minister` MEANS
