@ref s 4(12) (src:1957-1962)
GIVEN `the provision in which the reference to the Minister appears` IS A STRING
      `the person is a Minister of State for the Minister's Ministry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has authorised the person to hear an appeal under that section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(12) the reference to the Minister includes the Minister of State` MEANS
    IF (NOT (elem `the provision in which the reference to the Minister appears` `s 4(12) the provisions in which a Minister of State may stand for the Minister`))
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of section 20(3), 27(2), (5), (5AA), (5A) or (12C), 28(3), (3D), (3DA) or (3E), 29(8A), 155B(8), 359(9), 360(3), 369(2), 377(13) or 378(5), (9) or (16)"
    ELSE (IF `the person is a Minister of State for the Minister's Ministry` AND `the Minister has authorised the person to hear an appeal under that section`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "any reference to the Minister includes a reference to a Minister of State for his or her Ministry who is authorised by the Minister for the purposes of hearing an appeal"

§ `Section 4(13): the memorandum and articles become the constitution`

-- src:1966 | (13) With effect from 3 January 2016 —
-- src:1968 | (a) the memorandum of association and the articles of
-- src:1969 | association of a company that are in force for the
-- src:1970 | company immediately before that date —
-- src:1972 | (i) are collectively deemed to constitute, and have effect
-- src:1973 | as, that company’s constitution; and
-- src:1975 | (ii) may be amended by the company from time to time
-- src:1976 | in the same manner as the constitution of a company;
-- src:1977 | and
-- src:1979 | (b) any reference in any written law and in any contract or
-- src:1980 | other document having legal effect to the memorandum of
-- src:1981 | association, or the articles of association, or both, of a
-- src:1982 | company is deemed to refer to the company’s constitution.
@ref s 4(13) (src:1966-1982)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the memorandum of association and the articles of association of the company were in force for it immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(13)(a)(i) the memorandum and articles in force immediately before 3 January 2016 are deemed to be the company's constitution` MEANS
    IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "With effect from 3 January 2016" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); before that day the deeming has not begun)
    ELSE (IF `the memorandum of association and the articles of association of the company were in force for it immediately before 3 January 2016`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) the memorandum of association and the articles of association of a company that are in force for the company immediately before that date" (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling, item (c))

@ref s 4(13) (src:1966-1982)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the memorandum of association and the articles of association of the company were in force for it immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(13)(a)(ii) the company may amend the memorandum and articles in the same manner as a constitution` MEANS
    IF `the date asked` AT LEAST `the day 3 January 2016` AND `the memorandum of association and the articles of association of the company were in force for it immediately before 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("may be amended by the company from time to time in the same manner as the constitution") whose gate ("With effect from 3 January 2016", the memorandum and articles in force) is not met; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork line F-S3 in NOTES.md)

@ref s 4(13) (src:1966-1982)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the reference is in a written law, or in a contract or other document having legal effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(13)(b) a reference to the memorandum or articles of association is deemed to refer to the company's constitution` MEANS
    IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "With effect from 3 January 2016" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))
    ELSE (IF `the reference is in a written law, or in a contract or other document having legal effect`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reference in any written law and in any contract or other document having legal effect" (a scope limit with no "only")
